    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0043" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 4/7–2947: Circular
                    telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Representatives in the American
                            Republics
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-29T02:00:00-04:00">July 29, 1947—2
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Depcirtel July 24. At meeting Governing
                    Board PAU yesterday positions of Govts on
                    participation Nicaragua in Rio Conference <pb facs="0044" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/>
                    were recorded. Thirteen countries opposed extension invitation to Lacayo regime
                    and five favored it.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d28-f1"/> Consequently no invitation
                    to Nicaragua will be issued by PAU. It was held
                    by Chairman that question Nicaraguan participation could again be broached if
                    conditions should be altered in Nicaragua before end Rio Conference, e.g., if
                    Govt recognized by majority American Republics should be established there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d28-f1" n="51" xml:id="d28-f1-content">
                <p>According to airgram A–101, August 4, 1947, to Tegucigalpa, the five countries
                    were: Argentina, Colombia, Costa Rica, Dominican Republic, and Paraguay (710
                    Consultation 4/7–3147).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
